WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.363
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): —and it should say it's recording up the top now. Yep.

2
00:00:06.363 --> 00:00:12.617
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So, as I mentioned in the email, I just record these so I'm not scribbling the whole time,

3
00:00:12.617 --> 00:00:18.872
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and it's only for me and Nadia, it doesn't go anywhere. Is that all right with you both?

4
00:00:19.494 --> 00:00:20.715
Jess Moretti: Yeah, totally fine.

5
00:00:21.374 --> 00:00:27.014
Aiden M: Yep. Sorry, can you hear me? I'm in the car park at work, the signal's a bit—

6
00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:32.447
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): You're a little bit crunchy, Aiden, but I can hear you. You're good.

7
00:00:35.725 --> 00:00:41.682
Aiden M: Okay, cool. I'll stay still. If I drop out just keep going with Jess, she knows everything anyway.

8
00:00:42.424 --> 00:00:43.909
Jess Moretti: That's not true.

9
00:00:44.207 --> 00:00:51.943
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Ha. Well, that's usually how it goes. How are you guys going? Did you get any of that storm last night?

10
00:00:51.943 --> 00:00:54.522
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): It was pretty wild over our way.

11
00:00:55.143 --> 00:01:01.973
Jess Moretti: Oh my God, yes. We had hail. Like, little hail, not the golf ball stuff, but Leo was absolutely beside himself,

12
00:01:01.973 --> 00:01:04.901
Jess Moretti: he thought the roof was going to come off.

13
00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:09.454
Jess Moretti: We've got the, um, the metal roof on the rental, so it's just deafening.

14
00:01:10.216 --> 00:01:12.883
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah, it's that time of year, isn't it.

15
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:20.216
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): I had a client in Carindale send me a photo of their car this morning, little dents all over the bonnet. Anyway.

16
00:01:20.216 --> 00:01:25.883
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Before we dive in, I'll just give you a quick bit about me and how this works,

17
00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:33.217
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and then I'm going to ask you a lot of questions, and then we'll talk about whether we're actually a good fit.

18
00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:35.883
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): There's no pressure at all on this call.

19
00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:40.883
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Some people talk to us and decide to do it themselves, and that's fine too.

20
00:01:41.356 --> 00:01:42.416
Jess Moretti: Sounds good.

21
00:01:43.232 --> 00:01:47.259
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So, I'm Tom, I'm one of the buyers agents at Halyard.

22
00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:55.314
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): It's a small team, it's Nadia, who started the business, me, and Jo who looks after all the admin and the paperwork

23
00:01:55.314 --> 00:02:01.904
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): side and basically keeps us both alive. I mostly cover the south side and out towards the bayside.

24
00:02:01.904 --> 00:02:07.762
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): My background's a bit different to most, I was a carpenter for, God, about twelve years,

25
00:02:07.762 --> 00:02:14.719
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): then I did building inspections for a while, and I've been doing this for just over four years now.

26
00:02:14.719 --> 00:02:21.675
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So I tend to be the annoying one at inspections who's lying on the floor looking at the stumps.

27
00:02:21.981 --> 00:02:29.770
Aiden M: That's actually really useful. That's one of the things that freaks me out, honestly, like not knowing what we're looking at.

28
00:02:30.329 --> 00:02:35.819
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah, look, most people don't, and why would you. So, tell me a bit about you guys.

29
00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:39.048
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Where are you at, what's prompting it, all of that.

30
00:02:39.466 --> 00:02:46.511
Jess Moretti: Okay, um. So we're renting in Cooper Roo at the moment, we've been there about two and a half years.

31
00:02:46.511 --> 00:02:50.386
Jess Moretti: It's one half of a duplex, it's fine, it's just small.

32
00:02:50.386 --> 00:02:54.966
Jess Moretti: And the landlord told us a few weeks ago they're going to sell,

33
00:02:54.966 --> 00:03:00.954
Jess Moretti: so our lease runs out at the end of February and they've said they won't renew it.

34
00:03:01.522 --> 00:03:05.268
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Right. So there's a bit of a clock on it.

35
00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:07.603
Jess Moretti: There's a clock on it.

36
00:03:07.603 --> 00:03:15.453
Jess Moretti: Which is, um, I mean we were going to buy anyway, it's just kind of forced our hand on the timing.

37
00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:19.756
Aiden M: We'd been talking about it for like two years.

38
00:03:20.054 --> 00:03:21.943
Jess Moretti: For like two years, yeah.

39
00:03:21.943 --> 00:03:29.500
Jess Moretti: And we've got the two kids, Mia's six, she's in Year 1, and Leo's three, and we've got a dog,

40
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.657
Jess Moretti: so we really just need more space. A yard. Proper yard.

41
00:03:34.265 --> 00:03:35.761
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): What sort of dog?

42
00:03:36.526 --> 00:03:39.534
Jess Moretti: She's a kelpie cross. Biscuit. She's a lot.

43
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.601
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Kelpies are always a lot. Okay so yard is non-negotiable, that's one I can tick straight off.

44
00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:49.225
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And have you owned before or is this the first one?

45
00:03:50.183 --> 00:03:55.533
Aiden M: We had a unit in Greenslopes. We sold it, what, end of last year?

46
00:03:56.297 --> 00:04:01.147
Jess Moretti: Yeah, end of last year. So that money's sitting in the offset at the moment.

47
00:04:01.603 --> 00:04:02.327
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay, great.

48
00:04:02.327 --> 00:04:10.293
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So not first home buyers, which just changes a couple of things on the stamp duty side, but we'll get to that.

49
00:04:10.293 --> 00:04:15.362
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And what sort of budget have you been working to? Just ballpark for now.

50
00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:20.270
Jess Moretti: So we've been saying around 1.3. Like, 1.3, 1.35 at the absolute outside.

51
00:04:21.001 --> 00:04:24.250
Aiden M: Yeah, that's the number we've been working off.

52
00:04:24.887 --> 00:04:27.491
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay. One point three, one point three five.

53
00:04:27.491 --> 00:04:32.372
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And is that purchase price or is that everything in, stamp duty and all that?

54
00:04:32.745 --> 00:04:35.537
Jess Moretti: Um. Purchase price, I think. Yeah. Purchase price.

55
00:04:35.939 --> 00:04:36.256
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay.

56
00:04:36.256 --> 00:04:43.224
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): We'll come back and kind of pressure test that a bit later, because I want to make sure it lines up with

57
00:04:43.224 --> 00:04:48.926
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): what you actually want to buy. So where have you been looking? Where's your head at with areas?

58
00:04:49.936 --> 00:04:53.030
Jess Moretti: So, honestly, if money was no object, Camp Hill.

59
00:04:53.030 --> 00:05:00.593
Jess Moretti: We go to the cafes up there on the weekends and I just love it, those streets with all the big trees.

60
00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.582
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah, everyone loves Camp Hill.

61
00:05:06.037 --> 00:05:08.298
Jess Moretti: But I'm guessing that's not happening.

62
00:05:08.689 --> 00:05:15.550
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Look, I'll be honest with you, at one point three, Camp Hill is going to be really hard.

63
00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:23.173
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): You'd be looking at something like a small three bed on a smaller block that needs a lot of work,

64
00:05:23.173 --> 00:05:26.604
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): or a unit, and that's not what you want.

65
00:05:26.604 --> 00:05:33.084
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Most of what's selling in Camp Hill now with a decent yard is well north of that.

66
00:05:33.084 --> 00:05:37.277
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So I wouldn't spend your weekends there, put it that way.

67
00:05:37.975 --> 00:05:45.461
Jess Moretti: Yeah. That's what I figured. So then like, Carina, Carina Heights, we've looked at a few in Holland Park, Mount Gravatt East.

68
00:05:45.461 --> 00:05:50.225
Jess Moretti: Aiden's work's at Eight Mile Plains so anything that way is good for him.

69
00:05:51.209 --> 00:05:58.616
Aiden M: The tech park, yeah. So as long as I can jump on the M1 or the Gateway I'm happy.

70
00:05:58.616 --> 00:06:05.243
Aiden M: I don't want to be going through, like, Logan Road at eight in the morning every day.

71
00:06:05.849 --> 00:06:09.444
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Fair enough. And Jess, what about you, where's work?

72
00:06:10.151 --> 00:06:16.752
Jess Moretti: I'm a physio, I'm at a clinic in Greenslopes, and I'm part time at the moment. Three days.

73
00:06:16.752 --> 00:06:22.252
Jess Moretti: But I'm going back up to four days in February when Leo starts kindy properly.

74
00:06:23.286 --> 00:06:28.232
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay. And schools, I assume that's a big one with Mia in Year 1?

75
00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:36.699
Jess Moretti: Yes. So she's at a school near us now, and she's happy there, but we're happy to move her if we move.

76
00:06:36.699 --> 00:06:40.238
Jess Moretti: I'd rather, like, I don't want to move her twice though.

77
00:06:40.238 --> 00:06:44.742
Jess Moretti: So wherever we buy, I want it to be the school she stays at.

78
00:06:47.717 --> 00:06:51.898
Aiden M: And the Mansfield High catchment. That's the one everyone talks about.

79
00:06:52.403 --> 00:06:59.162
Jess Moretti: Yeah, for later. I mean she's six. But everyone says you need to think about it now.

80
00:07:00.002 --> 00:07:01.652
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah, look, they're not wrong.

81
00:07:01.652 --> 00:07:08.911
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): That catchment does carry a premium, and it's one of those things where if you're going to be there ten years it

82
00:07:08.911 --> 00:07:14.521
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): does matter. It also means you're competing with a lot of other families for the same houses.

83
00:07:14.521 --> 00:07:21.451
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So it's not a dealbreaker either way but I just want you to know it's a factor that pushes prices up.

84
00:07:21.451 --> 00:07:25.081
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Is it a must or is it a nice to have?

85
00:07:25.965 --> 00:07:28.476
Jess Moretti: Um. Nice to have? Is that—Aiden?

86
00:07:29.447 --> 00:07:32.660
Aiden M: I'd say like a strong nice to have.

87
00:07:33.601 --> 00:07:39.465
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): A strong nice to have. I'm writing that down exactly like that. Okay, so the house itself.

88
00:07:39.465 --> 00:07:41.535
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Bedrooms, bathrooms, what are you picturing?

89
00:07:42.251 --> 00:07:43.429
Jess Moretti: Four bedrooms ideally.

90
00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:51.674
Jess Moretti: Or three and a study, because I do some admin from home and Aiden works from home a couple of days.

91
00:07:52.719 --> 00:07:53.981
Aiden M: Two days, usually.

92
00:07:54.819 --> 00:08:00.806
Jess Moretti: Two bathrooms. Two is really important, the duplex has one and it's chaos in the morning.

93
00:08:01.123 --> 00:08:02.629
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yep. Land size?

94
00:08:03.264 --> 00:08:07.190
Aiden M: I mean, the bigger the better. Like at least five hundred?

95
00:08:07.931 --> 00:08:09.893
Jess Moretti: Six hundred would be nice.

96
00:08:10.383 --> 00:08:18.147
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Around Carina and Carina Heights you'll see a lot of six hundred and seven hundred square metre blocks, which is good,

97
00:08:18.147 --> 00:08:21.844
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): a lot of the older post-war houses are on those.

98
00:08:21.844 --> 00:08:28.868
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Mansfield and Wish art, a lot of them are seven hundred ish too. Are you set on a style?

99
00:08:28.868 --> 00:08:31.825
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Like, older house, newer house, renovated, needs work?

100
00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:39.496
Jess Moretti: I love the old ones. Like the post-war ones, the high sets with the, um, the battens underneath.

101
00:08:40.008 --> 00:08:43.240
Aiden M: And I like stuff that doesn't need work.

102
00:08:44.135 --> 00:08:45.995
Jess Moretti: He likes the brick lowsets.

103
00:08:46.712 --> 00:08:53.359
Aiden M: I do like a brick lowset. Low maintenance, you know. You know where you are with brick.

104
00:08:54.279 --> 00:09:00.779
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Ha, yeah, they're solid. Honestly, both are fine, and in your budget you'll be seeing a mix of both.

105
00:09:00.779 --> 00:09:04.884
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Can either of you do renovating? Like is that on the table?

106
00:09:05.356 --> 00:09:10.441
Jess Moretti: Cosmetic. Paint, maybe a kitchen down the track. Not, like, raising it or anything.

107
00:09:10.863 --> 00:09:13.846
Aiden M: Not with two kids and a dog, no.

108
00:09:14.349 --> 00:09:20.524
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): That's sensible. Okay, what about things you definitely don't want? This is actually the bit I find most useful.

109
00:09:23.143 --> 00:09:30.393
Jess Moretti: Main roads. I don't want to be on Old Cleveland Road or anything like that, with the kids.

110
00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.862
Aiden M: Power lines, the big ones.

111
00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:36.802
Jess Moretti: Yeah. Um, not flood. Definitely not anything that's flooded.

112
00:09:36.802 --> 00:09:44.364
Jess Moretti: We had friends in, um, in the 2022 floods, they were in Norman Park, and it was just awful.

113
00:09:44.804 --> 00:09:51.333
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah. So that one's really important around where you're looking, because you've got Bulimba Creek running through,

114
00:09:51.333 --> 00:09:59.015
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and a bunch of smaller creeks and gullies through Carina and Carindale, and then Norman Creek on the other side.

115
00:09:59.015 --> 00:10:05.545
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Part of what I do for every property is pull the council flood map and the overlays,

116
00:10:05.545 --> 00:10:13.995
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and look at whether it actually went under in '11 or '22, which is not always the same thing as what the

117
00:10:13.995 --> 00:10:20.908
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): map says. Some streets are on the overlay and were fine, and some, you know, the other way.

118
00:10:21.516 --> 00:10:23.270
Jess Moretti: I didn't know that.

119
00:10:24.287 --> 00:10:26.801
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah, the map's a guide. Pools?

120
00:10:28.903 --> 00:10:34.011
Jess Moretti: Ugh. I don't really want one, with Leo. But if it's fenced, I don't know.

121
00:10:34.478 --> 00:10:36.121
Aiden M: I'd love a pool.

122
00:10:36.862 --> 00:10:40.791
Jess Moretti: You'd love a pool until you have to clean it.

123
00:10:41.766 --> 00:10:42.793
Aiden M: That's fair.

124
00:10:43.147 --> 00:10:49.602
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): I'll put pool as a "don't care, don't want to pay extra for it." Is that about right?

125
00:10:50.153 --> 00:10:51.213
Jess Moretti: Yeah. Perfect.

126
00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:58.063
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay. So what have you actually done so far? Have you been to opens, made any offers?

127
00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:02.275
Aiden M: We've been going to opens since about, like, August?

128
00:11:02.695 --> 00:11:07.966
Jess Moretti: Yeah, since winter. Probably been through, I don't know, twenty houses? We went to two auctions.

129
00:11:07.966 --> 00:11:10.601
Jess Moretti: One in Holland Park, one in Karina Heights.

130
00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:13.173
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): How did those go?

131
00:11:14.108 --> 00:11:18.557
Jess Moretti: We didn't bid. We were just, like, watching. We were scared.

132
00:11:19.247 --> 00:11:25.503
Aiden M: The Holland Park one went for way more than what the agent had been saying, like way more.

133
00:11:25.503 --> 00:11:31.064
Aiden M: The agent said, um, buyers in the high ones, and it went for 1.48 or something.

134
00:11:31.961 --> 00:11:38.822
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah. That's really common at the moment, and I'll be honest, it's one of the main reasons people come to us.

135
00:11:38.822 --> 00:11:43.069
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): The guides can be pretty, let's say, optimistic. Do you remember which street?

136
00:11:43.587 --> 00:11:48.248
Aiden M: Um, it was off Abbots Lee? Near the Holland Park shops. Jess?

137
00:11:48.911 --> 00:11:55.024
Jess Moretti: I don't remember the street. It was the blue one. The one with the frangipani out the front.

138
00:11:56.031 --> 00:12:00.405
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Ha. I'll see if I can find it. Anyway, that's a good segue actually.

139
00:12:00.405 --> 00:12:03.529
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So you said one point three, one point three five.

140
00:12:03.529 --> 00:12:10.402
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Let me just be straight with you about what that buys, because I don't want you to go away with the wrong

141
00:12:10.402 --> 00:12:15.713
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): idea. In Carina and Carina Heights at one point three, you're probably looking at a three bed,

142
00:12:15.713 --> 00:12:22.587
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): maybe a three bed with a study, on a decent block, but often it needs some work or it's a bit original.

143
00:12:22.587 --> 00:12:29.460
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): A renovated four bed, two bath in Carina with a good yard, I'd honestly be expecting that to go one point four

144
00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.959
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): five, one point five plus at the moment.

145
00:12:32.386 --> 00:12:33.150
Jess Moretti: Yeah.

146
00:12:33.911 --> 00:12:41.008
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): In Mansfield and Wishart, one point three gets you more house, often a four bed brick lowset from the seventies or eighties,

147
00:12:41.008 --> 00:12:46.814
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): maybe with the kitchen and bathrooms done. Mount Gravatt East, similar sort of story, maybe a touch cheaper.

148
00:12:46.814 --> 00:12:52.298
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Holland Park, it's somewhere in between, depends a lot on which side of Logan Road you are.

149
00:12:52.298 --> 00:12:56.491
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So it's absolutely doable, it's just about which compromise you want to make.

150
00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:02.536
Aiden M: Can I, um. Can I just jump in? I think we sort of undersold it before.

151
00:13:02.952 --> 00:13:03.595
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Sure.

152
00:13:04.304 --> 00:13:09.587
Aiden M: So we've got pre-approval through a broker, and it's actually, like, it's more than that.

153
00:13:09.587 --> 00:13:13.109
Aiden M: I think Jess is being conservative, which is fair, but—

154
00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.443
Jess Moretti: I'm not being conservative, I'm being realistic.

155
00:13:17.106 --> 00:13:24.027
Aiden M: Okay, yeah, sorry, you're being realistic. But the broker had us, what was it, the borrowing amount was one point one,

156
00:13:24.027 --> 00:13:29.630
Aiden M: and then we've got about four hundred and twenty in the offset from the unit and savings.

157
00:13:30.273 --> 00:13:36.666
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay. So on paper you're at about one point five two of total funds, before costs.

158
00:13:37.247 --> 00:13:40.303
Aiden M: Yeah. And then stamp duty comes out of that.

159
00:13:40.932 --> 00:13:46.701
Jess Moretti: And I just, I don't want to be maxed out. Like, I want something left over.

160
00:13:46.701 --> 00:13:52.471
Jess Moretti: Childcare's still, like, a lot until Leo's at school, and I don't know, if something happens.

161
00:13:53.441 --> 00:14:01.016
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): No, that's completely fair, and honestly I'd always rather someone buys a bit under their max than sits right on it.

162
00:14:01.016 --> 00:14:07.508
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Can I give you a rough sense of the costs so you can see where the number lands?

163
00:14:07.508 --> 00:14:11.476
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): This is rough, Jo will do a proper one for you.

164
00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:13.388
Jess Moretti: Yes please.

165
00:14:13.657 --> 00:14:21.758
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So as a non first home buyer, owner occupier, stamp duty in Queensland on one point three is going to be roughly

166
00:14:21.758 --> 00:14:26.176
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): forty-eight thousand. At one point four five, it's more like fifty-six, fifty-seven.

167
00:14:26.176 --> 00:14:33.909
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Then you've got conveyancing, maybe two to two and a half grand, building and pest is usually six to eight hundred,

168
00:14:33.909 --> 00:14:39.064
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and you've got our fee if you go with us, which I'll go through.

169
00:14:39.064 --> 00:14:47.165
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So from your one point five two, if you bought at one point four five, you'd be pretty close to the line.

170
00:14:47.673 --> 00:14:51.523
Aiden M: Right, so one point four five is basically the max max.

171
00:14:52.358 --> 00:14:57.980
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): That would be the absolute max, and I wouldn't love it for you, to be honest.

172
00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:00.440
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): You'd want a bit of a buffer.

173
00:15:00.849 --> 00:15:03.211
Jess Moretti: See, this is what I mean.

174
00:15:03.791 --> 00:15:10.300
Aiden M: Yeah, no, I get it. But one point three is, like, a long way under the max.

175
00:15:11.055 --> 00:15:16.937
Jess Moretti: It is. Okay. Um. Can we—sorry, Tom, can we just talk about this for a sec?

176
00:15:17.677 --> 00:15:22.811
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Of course. Take your time, I'll just, I'll mute myself for a sec.

177
00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:32.252
Jess Moretti: Okay, you can come back.

178
00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.317
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): I'm back.

179
00:15:34.674 --> 00:15:41.284
Jess Moretti: Okay, so, I think what we're saying, and Aiden correct me, is like, we'd go up to one point four,

180
00:15:41.284 --> 00:15:44.259
Jess Moretti: maybe one point four five for the right house.

181
00:15:44.259 --> 00:15:50.538
Jess Moretti: But we'd want to be paying, like, one point three five, one point four. That's where we'd be comfortable.

182
00:15:50.866 --> 00:15:53.426
Aiden M: Yeah. That's it. For the right one.

183
00:15:53.426 --> 00:15:59.643
Aiden M: Like if it's the four bedder with the yard and it's in the catchment and all that.

184
00:15:59.994 --> 00:16:02.120
Jess Moretti: And it's not going to flood.

185
00:16:02.531 --> 00:16:04.899
Aiden M: And it's not going to flood.

186
00:16:05.242 --> 00:16:09.541
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay, so let me just play that back so I've got it right.

187
00:16:09.541 --> 00:16:13.510
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Ceiling's one point four five, that's purchase price, stamp duty on top.

188
00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:19.794
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): But really you want to be landing around one point three five to one point four. Is that right?

189
00:16:20.593 --> 00:16:25.693
Jess Moretti: Yeah. God, I can't believe I'm saying one point four five. But yeah.

190
00:16:25.973 --> 00:16:31.178
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Ha. That's normal. Everyone's number goes up. Honestly though, that changes things a fair bit.

191
00:16:31.178 --> 00:16:38.812
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): It brings the renovated stuff in Mansfield and Wishart well into range, it brings a lot of Carina and Carina Heights into

192
00:16:38.812 --> 00:16:45.405
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): range, and Holland Park you're competitive. It also means you're not sweating every auction going twenty grand over guide.

193
00:16:45.772 --> 00:16:48.412
Aiden M: Yeah, that's what I was thinking.

194
00:16:49.454 --> 00:16:54.509
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And the broker, is the pre-approval current? They're usually good for ninety days.

195
00:16:55.521 --> 00:16:59.014
Aiden M: I think we got it in, like, September. Mid September.

196
00:16:59.637 --> 00:17:05.657
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay, so that's going to be getting close to running out, I'd ask them to refresh it,

197
00:17:05.657 --> 00:17:13.092
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): especially with Jess going back to four days, that might actually help. And send it to me when you've got it.

198
00:17:13.092 --> 00:17:18.403
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): It's just one of those things you want sorted before you're standing at an auction.

199
00:17:18.664 --> 00:17:20.465
Jess Moretti: Okay. I'll message him tonight.

200
00:17:21.078 --> 00:17:28.927
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Great. So let me tell you a bit about how we actually work, and then you can ask me whatever you want.

201
00:17:28.927 --> 00:17:31.424
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Is that okay? Aiden, how's your signal?

202
00:17:31.806 --> 00:17:38.782
Aiden M: Still here. A guy just parked next to me and he's staring at me talking to myself.

203
00:17:39.674 --> 00:17:44.782
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Ha. Classic. So the main thing we do is what we call full search and acquisition.

204
00:17:44.782 --> 00:17:48.613
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So basically, from where we are now, to you getting the keys.

205
00:17:48.613 --> 00:17:55.637
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): The first step is we sit down properly, usually in person, and go through all of this in way more detail and

206
00:17:55.637 --> 00:17:57.553
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): build what we call the brief.

207
00:17:57.553 --> 00:18:03.300
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So it's your must haves, your nice to haves, your dealbreakers, which streets, which streets not, all that.

208
00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:07.770
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Then we go out and search. And that's not just what's on the portals.

209
00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:12.878
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): A big chunk of what we buy, I'd say maybe a third, sometimes a bit more,

210
00:18:12.878 --> 00:18:19.902
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): is stuff that's either off market or it's pre-market, so the selling agent's about to list it and they call us first

211
00:18:19.902 --> 00:18:22.456
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): because they know we've got a qualified buyer.

212
00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:26.939
Jess Moretti: How does that work, like, why would they call you?

213
00:18:27.833 --> 00:18:29.426
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Because it's easy for them.

214
00:18:29.426 --> 00:18:36.433
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): If I ring an agent and say I've got a family with finance sorted, they're ready to go, here's what they want,

215
00:18:36.433 --> 00:18:41.848
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): a lot of agents would rather do a quick clean deal than run a whole four-week campaign.

216
00:18:41.848 --> 00:18:46.944
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Not always, and the seller still has to agree to it, but it happens a lot.

217
00:18:46.944 --> 00:18:52.677
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Especially coming into Christmas, actually, when a lot of sellers don't want to be doing opens in December.

218
00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:54.363
Aiden M: Huh.

219
00:18:55.316 --> 00:19:00.211
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So then, when something comes up that fits, I go and look at it first.

220
00:19:00.211 --> 00:19:06.085
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): I'll often do a video walkthrough for you, I'll check the things I mentioned, the flood maps, overlays,

221
00:19:06.085 --> 00:19:11.959
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): I'll look at the roof, the stumps, whatever. And I'll tell you if I think it's a dud.

222
00:19:11.959 --> 00:19:18.485
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): That saves you most of the Saturday running around. When there's one that's worth it, you come and see it.

223
00:19:18.485 --> 00:19:21.748
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): If you like it, we do the numbers on it.

224
00:19:21.748 --> 00:19:28.274
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So I'll pull the comparable sales and tell you what I think it's actually worth, not what the agent says,

225
00:19:28.274 --> 00:19:33.169
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and what I think it'll take to buy it, which isn't always the same thing.

226
00:19:33.744 --> 00:19:34.391
Jess Moretti: Right.

227
00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:40.606
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And then I negotiate it, or I bid for you at auction.

228
00:19:40.606 --> 00:19:46.352
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Then we get it under contract, and I work with your conveyancer or solicitor on the conditions,

229
00:19:46.352 --> 00:19:50.746
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): organise the building and pest with an inspector we trust, all of that.

230
00:19:50.746 --> 00:19:56.154
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And then I'm there, well, not there, but I'm in the mix right through to settlement.

231
00:19:56.590 --> 00:20:04.100
Jess Moretti: Can I ask, um, with the contract stuff, I've heard there's some new thing with the seller having to give you documents

232
00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:04.441
Jess Moretti: now?

233
00:20:05.219 --> 00:20:11.749
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah, so since August last year, sellers in Queensland have to give you a disclosure statement before you sign.

234
00:20:11.749 --> 00:20:17.591
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): It's got things like the title, any easements, the rates, flood info in some cases, pool compliance,

235
00:20:17.591 --> 00:20:24.464
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): body corporate stuff if it's a unit. It's actually really good, it means we see a lot more up front.

236
00:20:24.464 --> 00:20:28.244
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): But you still need to read it properly, and people don't.

237
00:20:29.294 --> 00:20:33.311
Jess Moretti: Okay. Good. And building and pest, you said you'd organise that?

238
00:20:36.268 --> 00:20:42.519
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yep. And on a private treaty sale here you've usually got your building and pest condition, your finance condition,

239
00:20:42.519 --> 00:20:46.138
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and then you've also got the five business day cooling off.

240
00:20:46.138 --> 00:20:50.415
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): At auction, none of that, it's unconditional on the fall of the hammer.

241
00:20:50.415 --> 00:20:54.364
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So if there's an auction, we do the building and pest before.

242
00:20:56.228 --> 00:21:01.686
Aiden M: Right, so you pay for an inspection on a house you might not even get.

243
00:21:02.137 --> 00:21:05.944
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Exactly. Which is annoying, but it's way better than the alternative.

244
00:21:05.944 --> 00:21:13.559
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): We usually get it done for a few hundred bucks less through our inspector, and I'll often go through it with them,

245
00:21:13.559 --> 00:21:16.328
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): so at least you know what you're buying.

246
00:21:17.351 --> 00:21:22.037
Jess Moretti: Okay. And um, sorry, the elephant in the room. How much do you charge?

247
00:21:22.934 --> 00:21:26.328
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Ha. Yeah, I was getting there. So there's two parts.

248
00:21:26.328 --> 00:21:31.079
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): There's an engagement fee upfront, which is two and a half thousand plus GST.

249
00:21:31.079 --> 00:21:36.848
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): That's paid when you sign up and it covers the brief and the start of the search.

250
00:21:36.848 --> 00:21:41.259
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And then there's a success fee, which is paid when you actually buy,

251
00:21:41.259 --> 00:21:48.046
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and that's one point eight percent of the purchase price plus GST, with a minimum of fifteen thousand plus GST.

252
00:21:48.046 --> 00:21:52.797
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And the engagement fee comes off the success fee, so it's not on top.

253
00:21:53.083 --> 00:21:57.097
Aiden M: So if we bought at one point four, that's, um—

254
00:21:57.180 --> 00:22:05.073
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): One point eight percent of one point four is twenty-five thousand two hundred, plus GST. Minus the engagement fee you've already paid.

255
00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:06.052
Aiden M: Okay.

256
00:22:06.781 --> 00:22:08.237
Jess Moretti: That's a lot.

257
00:22:08.935 --> 00:22:11.908
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): It is. I'm not going to pretend it's not.

258
00:22:11.908 --> 00:22:18.846
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): The way I'd think about it is, does it save you that, or more, between price and avoiding a mistake and,

259
00:22:18.846 --> 00:22:22.810
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): you know, your time. Most people we work with say it did.

260
00:22:22.810 --> 00:22:29.086
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): But I always say, if you're confident doing it yourself, do it yourself. Some people are great at it.

261
00:22:29.347 --> 00:22:33.358
Jess Moretti: No, it's not, I'm not saying no. It's just, yeah.

262
00:22:34.211 --> 00:22:40.592
Aiden M: The Holland Park auction, we would have paid, like, a hundred grand too much, if we'd got that one.

263
00:22:40.882 --> 00:22:46.347
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Ha. Maybe. Maybe not, sometimes things are worth what they go for. But yeah, that's the idea.

264
00:22:47.321 --> 00:22:52.622
Jess Moretti: Do you get anything from the selling agent? Like a commission or a referral?

265
00:22:53.067 --> 00:22:56.930
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): No. Never. We're only paid by you, and that's in the agreement.

266
00:22:56.930 --> 00:23:04.013
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): If a selling agent ever offered me something I'd have to disclose it to you anyway, but we just don't take it.

267
00:23:04.013 --> 00:23:05.623
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): It would be a conflict.

268
00:23:06.247 --> 00:23:09.914
Jess Moretti: Okay, that's good. That was one I was going to ask.

269
00:23:09.914 --> 00:23:14.913
Jess Moretti: My sister used one in Sydney and she wasn't sure who they were working for.

270
00:23:15.255 --> 00:23:21.691
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah, there's a bit of that around. We're very, very clear on it. Any other questions so far?

271
00:23:21.983 --> 00:23:26.764
Aiden M: Um. How long does it usually take? Like, with the February thing.

272
00:23:27.549 --> 00:23:34.127
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): It varies a lot. If the brief is realistic, which I think yours is now with the bump,

273
00:23:34.127 --> 00:23:41.070
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): I'd say typically six to ten weeks to get something under contract. Sometimes it's two weeks, sometimes it's longer.

274
00:23:41.070 --> 00:23:47.648
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): The thing to know is the market goes pretty quiet from mid December through to, like, late January.

275
00:23:47.648 --> 00:23:50.206
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): There's still stuff happening, but less listings.

276
00:23:50.206 --> 00:23:56.418
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): So realistically, there's the next five or six weeks before Christmas, and then February's normally really busy.

277
00:23:57.004 --> 00:24:02.257
Jess Moretti: So if we started now, we might be able to get something before Christmas?

278
00:24:03.269 --> 00:24:05.101
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Might. I wouldn't promise it.

279
00:24:05.101 --> 00:24:12.061
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And then, settlement's usually thirty to sixty days, so if you bought in January you could settle in Feb,

280
00:24:12.061 --> 00:24:18.654
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): if you bought in early Feb it'd be tight but we can sometimes ask for a short settlement.

281
00:24:18.654 --> 00:24:24.149
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Worst case, a lot of people do a month or two on a short lease.

282
00:24:25.113 --> 00:24:27.717
Jess Moretti: Ugh, I don't want to move twice.

283
00:24:28.184 --> 00:24:34.945
Aiden M: We might be able to ask the landlord for an extra month, they might not have sold by then.

284
00:24:35.701 --> 00:24:42.469
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): That's worth asking. Okay, other things I should ask you. Is there anyone else involved in the decision?

285
00:24:42.469 --> 00:24:45.853
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Parents helping, anyone you need to run it past?

286
00:24:46.886 --> 00:24:51.150
Jess Moretti: No. Well, my mum will have opinions, but she's not paying for anything.

287
00:24:51.448 --> 00:24:58.074
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Ha. Mums always have opinions. Okay. Anything else on the house, like, is a garage important? Off-street parking?

288
00:24:58.406 --> 00:25:06.898
Aiden M: Two cars. I've got the ute, so a carport at least. A garage would be good for, like, the bikes and stuff.

289
00:25:07.689 --> 00:25:11.114
Jess Moretti: And a kitchen that's not tiny. I don't need fancy.

290
00:25:11.114 --> 00:25:16.939
Jess Moretti: Just, like, I want to be able to see the yard from the kitchen. Watch the kids.

291
00:25:17.571 --> 00:25:22.381
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): That's a really common one. Open plan, kitchen looking out to the yard.

292
00:25:22.381 --> 00:25:27.191
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Northerly aspect for the back is nice too, if we can get it.

293
00:25:28.112 --> 00:25:30.412
Jess Moretti: What does that mean, sorry?

294
00:25:31.161 --> 00:25:35.241
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Oh, sorry, so it's about which way the back yard faces.

295
00:25:35.241 --> 00:25:40.804
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): In Brisbane you want your living areas and yard facing north or north east ideally,

296
00:25:40.804 --> 00:25:44.142
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): you get the winter sun and the summer breeze.

297
00:25:44.142 --> 00:25:50.448
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): It's not a dealbreaker, it just affects how a house feels, and actually affects value a bit.

298
00:25:50.904 --> 00:25:56.917
Jess Moretti: Oh. Okay. I hadn't thought about that. Our duplex faces west and it's like an oven.

299
00:25:57.958 --> 00:26:00.758
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Yeah, the west ones in summer are rough.

300
00:26:00.758 --> 00:26:06.358
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay, so the other thing I wanted to ask, how flexible are you on the suburbs?

301
00:26:06.358 --> 00:26:10.208
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Because, like, Carindale, Belmont, are those on your radar at all?

302
00:26:11.194 --> 00:26:13.843
Aiden M: Belmont's a bit far out for Jess.

303
00:26:14.793 --> 00:26:22.546
Jess Moretti: Belmont's lovely, but it's sort of, it's just a bit out of the way for everything we do. Carindale, maybe?

304
00:26:22.546 --> 00:26:27.198
Jess Moretti: Is that, like, near the shopping centre, is it all a bit?

305
00:26:27.836 --> 00:26:35.619
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Some parts are great, some parts are a bit main road heavy. It's a big suburb. And it's got the creek.

306
00:26:35.619 --> 00:26:40.067
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): I'd say let's keep it as a maybe. Could go either way.

307
00:26:40.378 --> 00:26:40.887
Jess Moretti: Okay.

308
00:26:41.380 --> 00:26:46.873
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Mansfield and Wishart, do they feel too far from the school stuff, or from Jess's work?

309
00:26:47.237 --> 00:26:53.049
Jess Moretti: No, I think that's fine, Greenslopes is only like fifteen minutes from there if the traffic's okay.

310
00:26:53.393 --> 00:26:55.212
Aiden M: Which it never is.

311
00:26:56.213 --> 00:26:59.418
Jess Moretti: Which it never is. But yeah, it's fine.

312
00:26:59.912 --> 00:27:05.977
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Okay. So I think I've got a pretty good picture. Let me tell you what happens next.

313
00:27:05.977 --> 00:27:13.470
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): I'll send you an email this afternoon, it'll have a summary of what we talked about, the fee stuff in writing,

314
00:27:13.470 --> 00:27:19.536
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and the agreement. In Queensland it's called a Form 6, it's the appointment form, plus our terms.

315
00:27:19.536 --> 00:27:23.818
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Have a read over the weekend, ask me anything. There's no rush.

316
00:27:24.783 --> 00:27:25.414
Jess Moretti: Okay.

317
00:27:25.955 --> 00:27:33.038
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): If you decide to go ahead, Jo will get it signed electronically and send the invoice for the engagement fee,

318
00:27:33.038 --> 00:27:38.704
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): and then we book in the brief session, which I'd like to do in person, ideally,

319
00:27:38.704 --> 00:27:44.017
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): maybe at your place or a cafe somewhere. Takes about an hour and a half.

320
00:27:44.017 --> 00:27:47.913
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And then I'd start sending you stuff pretty much straight away.

321
00:27:48.614 --> 00:27:52.445
Aiden M: Can we do it on a weekend? The brief thing?

322
00:27:53.145 --> 00:27:59.745
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Saturday mornings are tricky because I'm usually at auctions or opens, but a Sunday or an evening is fine.

323
00:28:01.994 --> 00:28:03.020
Jess Moretti: Sunday's good.

324
00:28:04.043 --> 00:28:04.367
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Great.

325
00:28:04.367 --> 00:28:11.494
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And also, in the email I'll put in three or four recent sales from Carina and Mansfield that I think are good

326
00:28:11.494 --> 00:28:15.706
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): comparisons, just so you can see what one point four ish actually buys.

327
00:28:15.706 --> 00:28:18.946
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): That might help you both get a feel for it.

328
00:28:19.633 --> 00:28:21.695
Jess Moretti: That would be really helpful.

329
00:28:22.535 --> 00:28:23.283
Aiden M: Yeah.

330
00:28:23.648 --> 00:28:30.072
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And then from you guys, the main thing is if you can chase the broker to refresh that pre-approval.

331
00:28:30.072 --> 00:28:34.805
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): And then flick it through. Doesn't need to be before you decide, just generally.

332
00:28:35.231 --> 00:28:37.350
Jess Moretti: Yep, I'll do that tonight.

333
00:28:37.916 --> 00:28:39.230
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Any last questions?

334
00:28:39.875 --> 00:28:42.228
Jess Moretti: Um. I don't think so. Aiden?

335
00:28:43.210 --> 00:28:47.100
Aiden M: No, I think that's it. That was really helpful, mate, thanks.

336
00:28:48.033 --> 00:28:51.364
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): No worries at all. Honestly, you're in a good spot.

337
00:28:51.364 --> 00:28:58.360
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): You've done the hard bit, you've got the deposit, you've got the pre-approval. It's just about finding the right one now.

338
00:28:59.376 --> 00:29:06.236
Jess Moretti: Thank you. Okay, um, we'll have a look at the email and come back to you early next week?

339
00:29:07.128 --> 00:29:10.810
Tom Kerrigan (Halyard): Perfect. Have a good weekend. Hope the hail stays away.

340
00:29:11.653 --> 00:29:13.268
Jess Moretti: Ha. Thanks, you too.

341
00:29:13.681 --> 00:29:15.246
Aiden M: Cheers, see ya.
